Vendor Contract Intake Checklist

1. Business information

* Business owner identified.
* Business purpose documented.
* Description of goods or services recorded.
* Expected contract start and end dates recorded.
* Budget owner identified.

2. Vendor information

* Legal entity name verified.
* Vendor contact details recorded.
* Supplier due diligence completed.
* Relevant certifications and insurance reviewed where applicable.

3. Commercial review

* Pricing and payment terms reviewed.
* Contract duration assessed.
* Renewal and termination provisions identified.
* Service levels and performance obligations documented.
* Liability and indemnity provisions referred for appropriate legal review.

4. Technology and data review

* SaaS or cloud service involvement identified.
* Access to company or customer data assessed.
* Data processing requirements identified.
* Security assessment requested where necessary.
* International data transfers identified for Privacy review.
* AI training and data usage provisions flagged where applicable.

5. Approval and execution

* Procurement review completed.
* Finance approval obtained.
* Legal review completed where required.
* Security and Privacy approvals obtained where applicable.
* Authorised signatories confirmed.
* Executed agreement stored in the approved repository.

6. Post-signature management

* Contract owner assigned.
* Renewal date recorded.
* Notice deadline recorded.
* Contract obligations monitored.
* Amendments and disputes documented.

Control principle: No contract should be treated as fully approved until all required reviews and authorisations have been completed.